Do not reuse, quote, inspect, or imitate upstream source or prose. Implement direct, clean-room,
stdlib-only code.

Imports are closed: use only urllib.request, urllib.error, urllib.parse, pathlib, json, os, and
tempfile when needed, plus generated real.yt_dlp facade/type modules and cott_runtime. Do not use
multiprocessing, multiprocessing.pool, threading, asyncio, executors, pools, workers, queues,
callbacks, dynamic imports, subprocesses, external distributions, or any concurrency abstraction.
All work is sequential.

Every result is deterministic for identical inputs. Do not add extractors, plugins, ffmpeg,
site-specific logic, retries, configuration files, or dependencies.

parse_batch_urls trims each line, ignores blank lines and lines whose left-trimmed form begins
with any nonempty configured prefix, and otherwise returns trimmed URLs in input order. Reject an
empty comment prefix as InvalidInput.

expand_playlist_ranges treats indexes as one-based, inclusive ranges. An empty range list selects
all items once in input order. Nonempty ranges are expanded in supplied range order, retaining a
selected item once per matching range. Reject first == 0, last == 0, first > last, or endpoints
outside the item list as InvalidRange.

plan_downloads preserves input order. A URL in archive is omitted. If break_on_existing is true,
stop before the first archived URL and set stopped_on_archive; otherwise continue through later
items. Archive matching is exact URL equality.

render_output_path recognizes only %(id)s, %(title)s, %(ext)s, and %(playlist_index)s. Substitute
missing_placeholder for every other field name. Reject malformed placeholder syntax as
InvalidTemplate. Do not sanitize, create, or inspect paths.

render_items uses compact UTF-8 JSON. Lines emits one item object per line with a final newline;
Single emits one JSON array and no final newline. Object keys are id, title, ext, playlist_index,
and url in that order.

Use CottList only through its public ABI: iterate directly (`for item in items`), test membership
with `item in items`, use `len(items)` and `items[index]`, and convert with `list(items)` or
`tuple(items)`. NEVER access `.values`; every BasedPyright missing-attribute error for `.values`
is forbidden.
Construct CottList only as `CottList(values=tuple(...))`, including empty collections as
`CottList(values=())`. For an empty CottList with a known element type, bind a concrete annotation
first (for example, `rows: CottList[Row] = CottList(values=())`); do not rely on empty-literal
inference or casts. Preserve concrete element types through loops: annotate empty CottList
accumulators and keep loop variables and derived collections typed rather than allowing Unknown
propagation.

transfer_media accepts only http:// and https:// URLs. In simulation, do no network or filesystem
work and return a receipt with zero bytes and simulated true. Otherwise make exactly one direct
urllib.request HTTP(S) request and synchronously stream it in bounded chunks to a sibling temporary
file. Before each write, reject a chunk whose accumulated size would exceed max_bytes. Create
destination parents, close the completed temporary file, then atomically os.replace it onto the
destination. Use direct temporary-path cleanup on every non-success path; never leave a temporary
file or partial destination. For strict typing, declare cleanup state exactly `temporary_path: Path | None = None` before assignment and guard cleanup with `if temporary_path is not None` after both exceptions and success; never compare a non-optional `Path` to `None`. Map malformed URLs to UnsupportedUrl, HTTP responses outside 200..299
to HttpStatus, transport failures to NetworkFailure, and filesystem failures to OutputFailure.
